  "description": "Installation of roof plant and associated ductwork/louvres.",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Induct attenuators shall be installed in the atmospheric intake and exhaust paths of all Air Handling Units (AHU) and Extract Fans (EF) as specified in Section 9.3 of the Environmental Noise Survey and Plant Noise Assessment Report (32192/PNA1-R5). The attenuators shall provide at least the minimum dynamic insertion loss (dB) at each octave band frequency as detailed in the aforementioned table.\r\rThe AHU S1 and AHU S2 shall be selected and installed such that the case breakout noise does not exceed a sound pressure level of 53 dBA at 1 metre, as specified in Section 9.3 of the report\r\rReason: To ensure that the proposed equipment operates in a way that does not give rise to material impacts on the local acoustic environment, in accordance with Policy D14 of the London Plan."
  ],
